{"id":"supervision","ord":"a0","title":"Supervision: the watcher and the mute list","desc":"**Everything goes through kolu** (graduated from instructions.md, 2026-08-25): never run, resume, or message an agent outside its kolu terminal — no headless `claude -p`, no `--resume` in a background shell, no side channels; a terminal that can't receive the instruction is a stop-and-ask. Kolu MCP is for ACTIONS only (spawn, read screens, send input, kill), always as instant calls; blocking MCP waits are banned from the supervision path.\n\n**The wake mechanism** (the one law): `kolu watch --states waiting,awaiting --held-for 60s --nag 10m --ignore <mute-list> --heartbeat 30m` run under the harness's Monitor tool with `persistent: true` (a background Bash task notifies only on exit — a watch stream never exits; RCA 2026-08-21). Fleet-wide, never an id list. It dies LOUDLY on server/process restarts: re-arm it, update the `watch-task` prop, record the re-arm here. THE RESTART DRILL is mechanical and keyed to the SIGNAL, not to memory (2026-08-26, after the human caught a missed re-arm): the moment a deploy/MCP-disconnect/stopped-task notice appears — re-arm the watcher, update `watch-task`, re-arm session crons (the soak check), verify own terminal id, before any other work. The orchestrator babysits every spawned terminal until its PR merges — on every wake: land the event on the board before working it, then work it to a flipped mark plus a dispatched next step (or an explicit block). No turn ends with an unread event or an unsupervised live lane.\n\n**The mute list's dispositions** (ruled 2026-08-23 ~17:15; 🔥 corrected 2026-08-24; ids rotate on kaval restart — re-identify by intent/cwd, never assume):\n- `d7543299` — WAS the orchestrator's own headless terminal; DEAD since the 2026-08-26 deploys — the chat panel's terminal has not re-registered with padi since (verified in kolu ls); re-identify and re-mute if it reappears.\n- `30f81ddc` 🔥 — the human's Fable agent on kolu, engageable on their word only.\n- `724a754e` — the human's nixos-config grok (+ its splits).\n- `8bb96ee1`, `52e990d4` — the human's spawns, currently absent from the fleet (dead ids, fail-open, kept for the record).\n- The GENERALIZED RULE: any terminal no lane's `terminal` prop names, outside olai's worktrees, is presumed the human's; one INSIDE olai's worktrees that the orchestrator did not create is the human's spawn until handed over. Mute only after the disposition is verified via kolu ls — never on assumption. Fail-open: a stale id costs nothing, every new terminal still rings.\n\n**Nag discipline** (RCA-2, 2026-08-21; HARDENED 2026-08-26 after the CI-launch lapse): a nag on an unchanged block is re-DERIVED, not re-acknowledged — a second nag with no new information means the block is suspect: act on standing authority or escalate as a standalone question. A dismissal applies to an event, never to a terminal. **EVERY nag response NAMES THE BLOCKER explicitly. \"Blocked on the human\" or \"blocked on agent X\" may stand; \"BLOCKED ON THE ORCHESTRATOR\" is illegal to leave standing — it converts to the action in the same turn.** The 2026-08-26 lapse: pi's done-report nagged three times while the orchestrator's own CI launch sat as a sentence; each nag was stamped \"known hold\" without asking waiting-on-whom.\n\n(Moved whole from agents.olai 2026-08-25 — supervision is process state, not a roster row; the old subtree `supervision-watcher` is in Trash. Standing rulings and dated history live in the children below.)","created":"2026-08-25T16:28:07-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T19:37:04-04:00","custom":{"mute-list":"d7543299, 30f81ddc, 724a754e, 8bb96ee1, 52e990d4","watch-task":"bg511a857"}}
{"id":"ci-venue","parent":"supervision","ord":"a0","title":"CI venue — the standing ruling","desc":"RULED by the human 2026-08-24 ~15:56 (supersedes the 2026-08-22 localhost-only ruling): kolu-ci-* boxes are back AND CAN BE USED — CI may dial them via odu's ordinary --platform path. Localhost (under `/tmp/olai-odu-localhost.lock`) and ci@petit for darwin (under `/tmp/olai-odu-petit.lock`) remain available; the once-mandatory `--host x86_64-linux=localhost` pin is lifted. For olai PRs EITHER platform green is the bar; kolu PRs need both. Admin merges are fine for a macOS-only-green olai PR (`gh pr merge --squash --admin`) — the GitHub ruleset still requires the nine x86_64-linux contexts and is deliberately not narrowed.\n\n**PARALLELISM (the human's correction 2026-08-26 ~10:10): CI runs PARALLELIZE across venues — never queue a second run on the localhost flock when the kolu-ci pool is free.** One run may hold localhost (flocked) while others dial the pool via bare `--platform`; the flock is a per-venue serializer, not a global one.\n\nHistory: the kolu-ci fleet was ABANDONED 2026-08-22 10:41 (Incus instability — boxes vanishing mid-e2e within ~30min of creation; the full failure transcript is https://gist.github.com/srid/143288f346ba71e27cfb54e67173e3b0), which forced the localhost/petit two-venue era, then un-abandoned 2026-08-24.","created":"2026-08-25T16:28:07-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T10:09:24-04:00"}
{"id":"kolu-pr-process","parent":"supervision","ord":"a1","title":"kolu PRs ride kolu's own process","desc":"RULED by the human 2026-08-22 16:15: kolu PRs are taken through KOLU's process — the author runs kolu's /be skill (.agents/skills/be/SKILL.md in the kolu checkout) instead of our review/refactor round, and CI through kolu's /ci skill (.agents/skills/ci/SKILL.md) instead of our odu recipe; both platforms green before merge; the orchestrator merges on /be done + /ci green. 16:20: the darwin host /ci names was replaced by ci@petit (--host aarch64-darwin=ci@petit, under /tmp/olai-odu-petit.lock). Olai PRs keep our process. First applied to lane-scli PR 1 (surface-cli-kolu).\n\n**AMENDED by the human 2026-08-25 ~20:40: /ci runs ONCE, when the PR is FULLY DONE** — never per amendment round. Amendment rounds carry typecheck/local suites only; the single both-platforms /ci fires when no further changes are coming (for a consumer-gated PR like kolu#2216: when the consumer compiles clean against the final head). The same one-CI philosophy olai lanes already run.\n\n**THE DRISHTI PAIR (the human, 2026-08-26 ~13:15): when kolu's paired-drishti-PR rule fires (package exports changed), the pair is ALWAYS opened — never waived, however additive the delta.** The kolu lane's author opens it (their brief extends to srid/drishti); the lane's progress reports mention the pair. First applied: kolu#2217's three added daemon-barrel exports.","created":"2026-08-25T16:28:07-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T13:18:21-04:00"}
{"id":"deploy-2026-08-21","parent":"supervision","ord":"a2","title":"2026-08-21: production deploy, double watcher death, full end-to-end verification","date":"2026-08-21","desc":"DEPLOYED ~21:20; the orchestrator's own process restarted ~21:25 — the watch died loudly both times as designed and was re-armed (bhb2ugljn). The second restart recycled every terminal id (the kolu skill's warning made real): the A/B experiment terminal died, every lane's terminal prop went stale, the mute list was rewritten.\n\nThen kolu#2194's FULL TEST with a real agent (terminal c01109d6, 21:28–21:35) — ALL STAGES PASSED: spawn+boot; typed prompt + Enter; READY in 1s; settle → test watch (--held-for 10s) transition arriving instantly (per-line flush verified); nag re-rings at exactly +45s/+90s; main watch (--held-for 60s) transition at +60s; second prompt → second transition; screen_text, kolu ls, --ignore mute list, --ignore-self, --heartbeat; loud death + re-arm twice; kill → terminal gone, state-knob watch silent by design. Verdict: GOOD — every claim exercised live on the production build.","created":"2026-08-25T16:28:07-04:00"}
{"id":"board-style","parent":"supervision","ord":"a3","title":"Board style: short titles, no stage scaffolding","desc":"The human, 2026-08-26, rulings while pruning the Kolu subtree:\n- **Titles stay SHORT** — \"I hate long ass titles being snipped with …\". A title is a name; context, rationale, and state live in the note. Retitled on the spot: \"PR: the terminal door — the `terminal` prop wears a live dot and opens…\" → \"The terminal door (#405)\".\n- **No pipeline-stage children on a lane** — \"don't understand why this child node is needed. terminal-door is the only active agent right now\". The implement/review/close stage children were process scaffolding; one node per lane, its note carrying the stage story. td-close and padi-status-header both folded into terminal-door's note and trashed. **Children that are an actual TODO list are fine of course** (the human, same day) — the rule is against ceremony, not against breakdown.\n- **The `terminal` prop lives on the parent node representing the lane** (the human, same day) — not on a stage child. The lane's node wears its agent's terminal.\n- **Day roots in lanes.olai get `set_done` when their day closes** (the human, same day: \"Why are they not 'done' so that Done:Hidden hides them?\") — a past day still unmarked sits in everyone's view forever. Eleven past days were marked in one sweep 2026-08-26; closing the day board is part of ending the day.","created":"2026-08-26T10:59:42-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T13:20:17-04:00"}
